description: PM OS operating contract. The shared policy lives in AGENTS.md; this rule only tells Cursor where to look and what the other harnesses enforce mechanically.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow @AGENTS.md (the PM OS operating contract) and @system/behavior-map.md (which surface owns which behavior). Cursor also loads `AGENTS.md` from the project root on its own; this rule is here so the policy applies even when that native read is disabled or truncated.

Hard rules that Amp and Claude Code enforce with hooks, which you must honor by convention here:

- Never run `git add -A`, `git add --all`, or `git add .`. Stage explicit paths.
- Never run `git push --force`, `git push -f`, or `git push --no-verify`. Never push at all unless the owner says so in this conversation.
- Confirm with the owner before `rm -rf` of anything outside `/tmp`, `$TMPDIR`, `node_modules`, `dist`/`build`, or this repository.
- Any Slack, GitHub, or email text you author on the owner's behalf opens with the bot attribution prefix defined in `AGENTS.md` (Bot Attribution Prefix).

Setting up or updating this install: apply `docs/install-decisions.md` (location, scope, Windows runtime, company tooling, Windows sidebar). Those choices are made; do not ask the owner.

Skills live in `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Cursor has no skill loader: when a task matches a skill description (index in `adapters/SKILLS.md`), open that `SKILL.md` and follow it before starting.
